WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:16.330
Fire And Blood will reign again and you can
expect to see the Robert's Rebellion in the

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.290
later
and final seasons of House of the Dragon!

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.200
The upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon, is based on the George

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.650
RR Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.490
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:38.330
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.950
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:47.500
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.050
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.910
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:00.660
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.539
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
In other words it covers events from Aegon's

00:01:05.539 --> 00:01:09.890
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:14.060
House of the Dragon will start with a build
up towards the Dance of the Dragons and early

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.229
seasons will cover the Dance itself. Later
seasons however, will be based on George RR

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:22.530
Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And Blood volume
2 book .

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:27.800
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:33.290
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:39.060
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.450
How do I know the second part of the Targaryen
history will cover all that? Because George

00:01:43.450 --> 00:02:32.610
RR Martin himself revealed it.
Fire And Blood volume 1 has 700 pages.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:38.590
In comparison, the book material Game of Thrones
show used was 4000 pages with the additional

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.730
summary from George RR Martin about the ending.
This prequel will last at least as long as

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:49.700
Game of Thrones and to achieve that, the showrunners
will use Fire And Blood volume 2 material

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:54.040
and as I already said, the main events of
it are the Blackfyre Rebellions and the Robert's

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.620
Rebellion so this is something you will see
on screen in the later seasons of House of

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.860
the Dragon.
Robert's Rebellion,also known as the War of

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.830
the Usurper, was a rebellion against House
Targaryen, primarily instigated by Eddard

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:11.040
Stark, Jon Arryn, and Robert Baratheon, for
whom it's named.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.400
It lasted "close to a year" and resulted with
the end of the Targaryen dynasty in the Seven

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.140
Kingdoms
and the beginning of Robert Baratheon's reign.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:24.620
It had 10 major battles and ultimately resulted
with the victory for the rebels, the end of

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.170
the Targaryen dynasty, and the start of the
Baratheon dynasty.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:33.730
In the prelude to the rebellion we have Tourney
at Harrenhal. After winning the final tilt,

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:38.390
Prince Rhaegar Targaryen was to crown the
new queen of love and beauty. Instead of crowning

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:44.150
his wife, the Dornish princess Elia Martell,
Rhaegar rode past her and crowned Lyanna Stark

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:49.340
of Winterfell instead who was bethroted to
Robert Baratheon. Eddard Stark would later

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:54.400
recall this moment as "the moment when all
smiles died". At the coming of the near year,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.010
the Starks received a message of Lyanna Stark's
abduction by Prince Rhaegar Targaryen near

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:04.360
Harrenhal. Her brother, Brandon Stark, was
on his way to Riverrun to wed Catelyn Tully,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:09.890
when the news reached him. Brandon rode at
once to King's Landing with his companions.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:15.390
Brandon rode for the Red Keep, and outside
its gates, unaware that Rhaegar was not present,

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:21.049
shouted for him to come out and die. King
Aerys II had them all arrested for plotting

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:26.130
the murder of the crown prince, and summoned
the fathers of all those who stood accused

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:31.220
to court. Lord Rickard Stark, who had been
on his way south with the wedding party for

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:36.560
Brandon's wedding, went to King's Landing
with two hundred men. None of them returned

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.620
north. In King's Landing, all of those who
stood accused were executed, with the sole

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:47.650
exception of Ethan Glover. King Aerys did
allow for trials, of a sort. Lord Rickard

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:52.669
Stark demanded a trial by battle, and the
king granted his request.

00:04:52.669 --> 00:04:57.490
Rickard dressed for battle, but Aerys declared
fire to be the champion of House Targaryen.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:02.840
He had Rickard suspended from the rafters
in the throne room, where his pyromancers,

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:08.241
kindled a blaze beneath the Lord of Winterfell.
Brandon Stark was brought in as well, and

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:14.950
placed in a Tyroshi strangling device, while
a longsword was placed just outside his reach.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:19.770
Brandon was allowed to try and free his father,
but more he struggled to reach the sword,

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:25.020
the tighter the cord around his neck became.
Brandon strangled himself in an attempt to

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:30.690
reach the sword and save his father, while
Lord Rickard cooked in his armor. Next, Aerys

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:35.639
demanded that Lord Jon Arryn sends him the
heads of Lord Robert Baratheon of Storm's

00:05:35.639 --> 00:05:41.000
End, Lyanna's betrothed, and Eddard Stark,
now the Lord of Winterfell after the deaths

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:47.060
of his father and older brother. Robert and
Eddard were Jon's wards at the Eyrie however,

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:52.550
and Jon instead raised his banners in revolt.
This act is seen as the start of the war,

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:58.090
which would last "close to a year". Not all
the lords in the Vale had sided with Jon Arryn,

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:03.289
and not all the lords in the stormlands sided
with Robert Baratheon. Robert himself firstly

00:06:03.289 --> 00:06:08.240
defeated those who sided with King Aerys in
the Vale and then fought and won 3 battles

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:14.240
in 1 day in the stormlands against those who
sided with King Aerys there. The next major

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.419
battle was the Battle of Ashford where Robert
Baratheon was defeated by Randyll Tarly which

00:06:19.419 --> 00:06:24.580
was the only defeat for Robert in the entire
war. Robert managed to escape capture with

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:28.720
the bulk of his forces.
Following the battle, Mace Tyrell marched

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:34.840
on Storm's End and laid siege to the castle.
Eddard Stark had managed to reach Winterfell,

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:40.449
where he called his banners. He marched south
with his forces, and joined up with Lord Jon

00:06:40.449 --> 00:06:46.620
Arryn. Together, they negotiated with Lord
Hoster Tully, the Lord of Riverrun for support.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:51.289
Meanwhile Hand of the King to the Mad King,
Jon Connington, led a mighty army into the

00:06:51.289 --> 00:06:57.490
field. The forces he commanded gave chase,
and Robert's march became a grueling one.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:02.650
Robert, wounded through unknown means, and
all alone, eventually took refuge at Stoney

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:05.620
Sept,
which would become the site of our next battle,

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:10.960
the Battle of the Bells. Jon Connington's
forces took the town by force and began to

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:16.470
search every house. The residents of the town
were actively helping Robert however, and

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:22.240
despite the search, then offered pardons,
rewards and threats, they could not find Robert.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:27.380
The battle began when Lords Stark and Tully
arrived with a rebel army. The soldiers fought

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:32.380
in the streets and alleys and on rooftops,
and septons rang the bells to warn the residents

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:37.840
to lock their doors. The battle was fierce,
and Jon Connington managed to wound Hoster

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:43.509
Tully and kill Jon Arryn's cousin, Ser Denys
Arryn. Eventually, Robert Baratheon came out

00:07:43.509 --> 00:07:48.690
of the Peach, the brothel in which he had
been hiding, and fought with Connington, almost

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:54.630
killing him. With both Elbert Arryn and Denys
Arryn now dead, Jon Arryn was in need of an

00:07:54.630 --> 00:08:02.139
heir. Hoster Tully swiftly betrothed his daughter,
Lysa, to Jon. In a double ceremony at Riverrun,

00:08:02.139 --> 00:08:07.949
Eddard Stark and Jon Arryn married Hoster's
daughters, Catelyn and Lysa, respectively.

00:08:07.949 --> 00:08:12.640
The crown prince finally returned from the
south and convinced Aerys to ask Tywin Lannister

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:18.870
for help, just as the rebels had or would
do, at one point. Additionally, Aerys commanded

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:24.621
his alchemists to place caches of wildfire
on multiple locations in King's Landing. After

00:08:24.621 --> 00:08:30.979
at first refusing to send aid to Aerys, both
due to his caution as well as due to his anger

00:08:30.979 --> 00:08:35.730
over Elia's treatment,
Prince Doran Martell agreed to send ten thousand

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:40.910
Dornishmen to strengthen the army Prince Rhaegar
Targaryen was gathering. The Battle of the

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:47.250
Trident was the next and decisive battle in
the war. Fought in 283 AC between the loyalist

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:52.890
and rebels, the battle took place at a place
known as the ruby ford since the battle, located

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:58.080
on the northern bank of the Trident, where
Rhaegar tried to cross the river. The loyalists

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:02.730
had forty thousand men, while the army of
the rebels numbered less men, who were more

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:08.760
battle hardened. Rhaegar and Lord Robert Baratheon
met in single combat with the battle raging

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:14.180
on all around them. Rhaegar managed to wound
Robert before Robert killed Rhaegar with a

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:20.110
blow to the chest from his warhammer. Eventually,
the Targaryen host broke and ran. Around the

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:24.990
time the Battle of the Trident was fought,
Robert proclaimed his intention to claim the

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:30.400
Iron Throne. Out of all three leaders of the
rebellion, Robert had the better claim, due

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:35.360
to the fact that his grandmother had been
Princess Rhaelle Targaryen, the youngest daughter

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:41.950
of King Aegon V Targaryen. To justify Robert's
claim, the maesters would later use his bloodties

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:47.000
to House Targaryen, although it was conquest
which won him the throne.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:51.610
Already prior to the Battle of the Trident,
King Aerys had been preparing his wildfire

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:58.380
plot. Aerys sent his wife, Queen Rhaella pregnant
with Daenerys along with his new heir, Prince

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:03.680
Viserys, to Dragonstone for safety. While
the Trident is seen by many as the decisive

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:09.350
battle of the war, the capital remained untaken
until the Sack of King's Landing when Tywin

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.951
Lannister showed up at capital to finish the
rebellion

00:10:11.951 --> 00:10:18.570
when Aerys hoped Tywin would help him. Upon
realization that all was lost, Aerys ordered

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:23.740
Rossart to ignite the wildfire caches throughout
the city, wishing to leave Robert nothing

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:29.510
but “ashes and bones”. He ordered Ser
Jaime Lannister, Lord Tywin’s eldest son,

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:35.910
to kill Tywin and bring his head to Aerys.
Instead, Jaime killed Rossart, and upon realization

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:41.079
that Aerys would simply give the order to
burn the city down to another pyromancer,

00:10:41.079 --> 00:10:45.841
returned to the Red Keep and killed Aerys
himself in the throne room while Tywin's men

00:10:45.841 --> 00:10:51.250
killed Rhaegar's wife and children. Robert
was pleased by these deaths, but Eddard was

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:57.830
furious. This resulted in an argument between
Eddard and Robert, and Eddard rode out alone

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:02.850
in anger to fight the final battles of the
war in the south. After lifting the siege

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:08.880
at Storm's End, Lord Eddard Stark rode further
south, to the tower of joy, and after battling

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:14.019
the legendary kingsguard, he found his sister
Lyanna dying after giving birth to Rhaegar's

00:11:14.019 --> 00:11:19.630
child. The final battle of the war was assault
on Dragonstone where the last Targaryens were.

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:25.350
Rhaella died giving birth to Princess Daenerys
Targaryen during a great storm that destroyed

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:30.520
the Targaryen fleet at anchor at the island.
With most of the Targaryen fleet destroyed,

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:36.090
and with the Baratheon fleet ready to take
Dragonstone, the household of the last Targaryen

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:42.510
stronghold was willing to sell the children
to the new king, Robert I Baratheon. Shortly

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:48.410
before Stannis sailed to Dragonstone, however,
Willem Darry and four loyal men smuggled Viserys,

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:53.740
Daenerys, and her wet nurse from the nursery
and sailed for the Braavosian coast, and the

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:59.170
children subsequently lived in exile in the
Free Cities. Following the conclusion of the

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:05.960
rebellion, Robert I Baratheon was successfully
installed as the new Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:11.029
Robert named his foster father, Jon Arryn,
as his Hand of the King. Robert had no wish

00:12:11.029 --> 00:12:16.370
to marry following the death of his betrothed,
Lyanna Stark, but Jon convinced him to marry

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:21.240
Lord Tywin Lannister's daughter, Cersei,
as the marriage would ensure Tywin's support,

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:26.470
should Viserys Targaryen ever attempt to win
his throne back. That's the story of the Robert's

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:29.149
Rebellion.
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed

00:12:29.149 --> 00:12:32.180
this video and if you did make sure to give
it a big thumbs up and I hope to see you in

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:32.480
the next one, peace!

